SUMMARY:The Rainbow Room: A young people's LGBTQ+ online space (for ages 1
 7-24)
DESCRIPTION:Awakening Asheville\nHosted by: Rainbow Mind\n**Register here/
 more info:** https://www.eventbrite.co.uk/e/the-rainbow-room-a-young-peopl
 es-lgbtq-online-space-for-ages-17-24-tickets-152074710553?aff=ebdssbonline
 search\n\nWelcome to the Rainbow Mind Young LGBTQ+ Rainbow Room. This is a
  welcoming and accepting space for young LBGTQ+ people aged 17-24 to conne
 ct\, share and explore mental health and wellbeing.\nThis group is not abl
 e to be a mental health crises support service. If you need more immediate
 \, intensive support please scroll down to the bottom of the page for info
 rmation.\n\n* This is an online queer space run by and for members who ide
 ntify as LGBTQ+\, or\, for those who exploring gender\, sexuality\, identi
 ty and relationship diversity.\n* At Rainbow Mind we also understand that 
 our identities and lives change and evolve and there is no need to feel yo
 u have to be a certain way\, or fit a certain box.\n* All parts of you are
  welcome.\n* Our team are experienced in creating safe online spaces for y
 oung LGBTQ+ people to meet\, connect\, share and support each other. Oh\, 
 and we really like music - so we'll be playing some of that too!\n* Input 
 always welcome and you are free to participate in the chat in any way you 
 feel safe to do so. Feel like turning camera off - that's fine\, feeling l
 ike you want to stay quiet - fine as well\, want to share a poem\, paintin
 g or magic trick - you are very welcome!\n* We will also be available to a
 nswer questions about the other forms of mental health support we have ava
 ilable here at Rainbow Mind.\n*\n\n**All members of the LGBTQ+ community a
 re invited\, whether you identify with an individual letter of the acronym
 \, more than one or are unsure of how you identify.**\nThank you and we lo
 ok forward to seeing you\,\nThe Rainbow Mind Young People Project Team\n*P
 lease note: this workshop is intended to be for LGBTQ+ young people aged b
 etween 17-24. Participants that do not fit this demographic will respectfu
 lly be asked to re-book on to a more appropriate event. bit.ly/TheGatherin
 gs*
